      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T08:19:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e exits silently\n\nFor this part, I don\u0027t think `skip_firstboot_after_datawipe` has to call `exit(0)` either. It can just return a bool? What confused me a bit was that I didn\u0027t find motivational difference in `skip_firstboot_after_datawipe` doing `exit` and `record` also exiting through returning `Ok(())` immediately after that.\n\nI don\u0027t feel the name of `skip_firstboot_after_datawipe` indicates the existence of any side effects either. How about renaming `can_perform_record` to `ensure_record_is_ready` or something that you feel doesn\u0027t imply the absence of side effects?",
      "parentUuid": "5c60fc2b_13d84324",
